course: dictionary
lesson: 8579
title: The schoolbag and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A schoolbag is made of two smaller words joined together: school and bag. When two words are joined like this, the new word often tells you about both parts. A schoolbag is a bag for school.
explain: The dictionary says a schoolbag is a bag a child uses to carry books, a pencil case, lunch and other things to and from school. A schoolbag can also be called a backpack or a satchel.
explain: Look at this sentence: «A boy in New Zealand called Tom kept a pile of cash in his schoolbag to show off; it was stolen at break, and he lost his birthday money.» The clue is in «stolen» and «lost»: things kept in a schoolbag can be taken, so it is wise to keep valuable things at home.
fact: A schoolbag is a bag a child uses to carry books, a pencil case, lunch and other things.
fact: A schoolbag is also called a backpack or a satchel.
fact: «Schoolbag» is a compound word, made from «school» and «bag».
fact: The plural of schoolbag is schoolbags: one schoolbag, two schoolbags.
fact: A heavy schoolbag can hurt your back, so wear both straps.
exercise: What is a schoolbag? | A bag for shopping at the supermarket | A classroom where children learn | A kind of shoe worn to school | *A bag a child uses to carry books, a pencil case and lunch
exercise: «Each schoolbag weighs 3 kg; what do 5 weigh?» | 35 kg | 8 kg | 2 kg | *15 kg
exercise: Which word is another name for a schoolbag? | Lunchtime | Blackboard | Playground | *Satchel
test: Tom kept a pile of cash in his schoolbag, and it was stolen at break. What is the best advice from his story? | Take your schoolbag home only at the weekend | *Do not keep lots of money in your schoolbag | Keep your birthday money in the classroom | Always leave your schoolbag open at break
test: A heavy schoolbag can hurt your back. What should you do? | Pack more books into it | Wear only one strap | Carry it in one hand all day | *Wear both straps
exam: «A two-year-old cannot zip up a schoolbag» tells you what? | Two-year-olds always carry schoolbags to school | Schoolbags are only for toddlers | Zips are only used at school | *A two-year-old is too small to do this job
